    "result_text": "Done. Full suite green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\nThe change adds `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present, else `PHONE`, following the codebase's existing computed-field pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared a `contactPreference` read-only property on the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto` at build time), mirroring the neighboring `locality`/`membershipLevel` fields.\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(owner.getEmail() != null ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\")\")` line to `toOwnerDto`, matching how `membershipLevel` already keys off `owner.getEmail() != null`.\n\nStructural impact was kept minimal: a single annotation line on an abstract interface method (CC 1, no method body to grow) plus a declarative schema addition \u2014 no logic added to any existing method body, and no new class needed since `OwnerMapper` is exactly the cohesive place these derived fields live.",
